{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Come, let me advise you.</b> R. Yochanan said: three were present at that counsel — Balaam, Job, and Jethro. Balaam, who advised — was killed. Job, who was silent — was sentenced to suffering. Jethro, who fled — his descendants merited and sat in the Chamber of Hewn Stone, as it is said: ״ומשפחות סופרים ישבו יעבץ תרעתים שמעתים סוכתים המה הקינים הבאים מחמת״ etc., and it is written: ״ובני קני חותן משה עלו מעיר התמרים״ etc. Another interpretation: איעצך — that is, regarding that matter concerning which you are afraid and tremble because of this assembly sitting opposite you — know that if you do not provoke them, do not fear them." "<b>That this people will do.</b> As is explained further on."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:07.794589594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}